ffalo shooter  and we see that it's cogent fascism  it is very much  a seemingly coherently  parroting and mirroring  the substance of the great replacement  theory etc stuff that we've seen  parroted by people like tucker carlson  on fox news and others  and yes to some degree we can also say  well most mentally ill people never  commit violence  and lots of people believe things that  are wrong there's an additional element  here  which certainly um could be a factor  nobody's denying that but we can't  ignore the very real kind of political  basis for the crime at least in terms of  the beliefs  in this case  this was an anti-vaxx pastor preacher i  guess preacher is the right word an  anti-gay preacher etc  but it seems very secondary to this  particular crime god told me to kill my  own wife  this case to create a contrast is the  point  it seems way more plausible to say the  main thing here  was some form of mental illness now of  course it's we're diagnosing from a  distance or not really not really  diagnosing but we're evaluating and  speculating from a distance in both  cases we would need to know more and  have more first-hand knowledge but the  point here is to say  when we cover up an incident by saying  it's only mental illness  we often intuitively say it doesn't  really make sense here these are the  perfect contrasts when we say well  mental illness for the buffalo shooter  very specific politically charged and  cogent manifesto  mental illness there has a very  obviously different meaning than in this  particular case where a guy allegedly  killed his wife because god told him to  not saying that there aren't multiple  factors to all of these stories but it  should at least allow us to see  how different the meaning of mental  illness can or might be in different  stories let me know if you agree with  the distinction i'm drawing here  uh in what are admittedly  tragic events  and very complicated events to  understand let me know your thoughts  w